{"id": "cd676f8909d691b32d2c", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/01_jira-requirement-analyzer/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/01_jira-requirement-analyzer/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "8d3c97df66f5ea1a91963a5b3dd40ccd0c1adaed", "sha256": "13a21282747744610a3eb4fa36921c53df4d673da88cbf1df3f14e97784a41e2", "bytes": 3424, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.516185+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/01_jira-requirement-analyzer/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/01_jira-requirement-analyzer/SKILL.md", "stlc_manual_testing/01_jira-requirement-analyzer/scripts/fetch_jira.sh"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: jira-requirement-analyzer\ndescription: >-\n  Read a JIRA ticket and judge whether it is actually ready to test. Use when a\n  tester says \"analyze this ticket\", \"is this story ready to test\", \"find gaps in\n  JIRA-123\", or pastes a user story / acceptance criteria and wants it pressure-tested.\n  Fetches the ticket, scores it against a readiness checklist, and returns a\n  gaps / ambiguities / risks report plus clarifying questions to send back to the author.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Requirement Analysis\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "jira-requirement-analyzer", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "e0c38c4c95c4900d9d72", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "fc5e2e266048d3ec84a77faf3df417dbafc26fab", "sha256": "7c9e09deb936a903c4cba9442f10542e5239d70a52dd78251f55cfc242f2ca0e", "bytes": 2047, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.516670+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/SKILL.md", "stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/context/How_to_Create_TestPlan_VWO.md", "stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/copilot/test-plan.prompt.md", "stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/references/requirement-checklist.md", "stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/scripts/fetch_jira.sh", "stlc_manual_testing/02_testplan-creater-via-jira_LIVE/template/test-plan-template.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-plan-generator\ndescription: \n  Turn a JIRA ticket into a review-ready test plan. Use when a tester or QA lead\n  says \"write a test plan for JIRA-1234\", \"plan testing for this story\", \"what should we test here\", or pastes an acceptance-criteria / user-story ticket.\n  Fetches the ticket, analyzes it for gaps and ambiguities, fills the standard\n  test-plan template, and stops for human review before anything is treated as final.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-plan-generator", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "3aa0d92380bb9676f63f", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/api-test-designer/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/api-test-designer/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "cb8f0bad548cad79ce3aeef73f5042e8011a0371", "sha256": "dd27a08fcfca912d5496e36e08bf18e4da94610f80459fbf8c4cdbb025b8b782", "bytes": 3162, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.516765+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/api-test-designer/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/api-test-designer/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: api-test-designer\ndescription: >-\n  Design API-level test coverage from an endpoint or contract. Use when a tester says\n  \"design API tests for POST /orders\", \"test this endpoint\", or pastes an OpenAPI /\n  contract snippet and wants coverage mapped. Produces a coverage matrix across happy\n  path, schema validation, auth/permission, negative inputs, boundary values, and\n  idempotency, each case tied to the contract, then stops for review before cases are built.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Design\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "api-test-designer", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "9a9ede1184be9b578104", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/test-scenario-designer/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/test-scenario-designer/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "d3738f6d47c35180621f13a8892fbb4626904d0c", "sha256": "7e3d33b8224f36e82227987a140e646b408979225a679bd423cc0169f54052d8", "bytes": 2963, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.516833+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/test-scenario-designer/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/03-test-design/test-scenario-designer/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-scenario-designer\ndescription: >-\n  Derive high-level test scenarios from a requirement or acceptance criteria before\n  anyone writes detailed steps. Use when a tester says \"what scenarios should we test\",\n  \"design scenarios for this feature\", or pastes ACs and wants coverage mapped out.\n  Produces positive, negative, boundary, and cross-role scenarios, each tagged by risk\n  and traced back to the AC it exercises, then stops for review before test cases are written.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Design\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-scenario-designer", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "fe643ae79d62b6947028", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-case-writer/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-case-writer/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "8d730bfac9449d7e6293d39a933faba8f3e5c2a1", "sha256": "6251d220178375e0cfdc801e785192e4866571a9d171ddd2f895184f1494de02", "bytes": 2842, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.516894+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-case-writer/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-case-writer/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-case-writer\ndescription: >-\n  Expand approved test scenarios into detailed, executable test cases. Use when a tester\n  says \"write test cases for TS-1\", \"detail these scenarios\", or hands over a reviewed\n  scenario list ready to become step-by-step cases. Produces preconditions, ordered steps,\n  expected results, and required data for each case, every one traceable to its scenario\n  and acceptance criterion, then stops for review before the cases are treated as final.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Case Development\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-case-writer", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "1524e60901acc0aadbb4", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-data-generator/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-data-generator/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "006ea6a09a9bd2c24fc3345903b5fda2c020375f", "sha256": "b98a680dc7471fe0b4c81ab4bb1dc9148fea25c53d6cd2a9d11baf59c69f38d2", "bytes": 2768, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.516960+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-data-generator/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/04-test-case-development/test-data-generator/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-data-generator\ndescription: >-\n  Produce the data sets a scenario or test case needs to run. Use when a tester says\n  \"generate test data\", \"give me boundary values for this field\", or needs valid,\n  invalid, boundary, and synthetic records to drive cases. Returns labeled data sets —\n  valid, invalid, boundary, and faker-style synthetic — each tied to the field or\n  scenario it exercises, with a note on which are safe to use in which environment.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: TheTestingAcademy\n  stlc-phase: Test Case Development\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-data-generator", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "ea127c14a15645d7bad7", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/automation-script-generator/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/automation-script-generator/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "2e061728c7019145412994f009bde6ce490ae511", "sha256": "3505cfd8339052b7dc71f8d49626146f6cbae17d537d39fa0169e0c06ebf4e00", "bytes": 2968, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517030+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/automation-script-generator/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/automation-script-generator/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: automation-script-generator\ndescription: >-\n  Turn an approved test case into a runnable automation script skeleton. Use when an\n  engineer says \"automate TC-5\", \"write a Playwright test for this\", or \"generate a\n  Selenium script from this case\". Produces a Playwright (TypeScript) or Selenium draft\n  using data-testid selectors and web-first assertions, mapped step-by-step from the case.\n  The output is a starting draft the engineer reviews, wires up, and runs — never a\n  finished test, and never assumes selectors or fixtures exist.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Execution\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "automation-script-generator", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "ba62c1609a8b856094d6", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/regression-suite-selector/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/regression-suite-selector/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "c428314d78fa499923f74ccd9a7775b07a47a97b", "sha256": "1238e31cc225896ddc1f7069bea6e3fc4c469b52a411d2fd33ebf724538fab99", "bytes": 2749, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517093+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/regression-suite-selector/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/regression-suite-selector/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: regression-suite-selector\ndescription: >-\n  Pick a targeted regression subset for a change instead of running the whole suite. Use\n  when an engineer says \"what regression should I run for this PR\", \"pick regression tests\",\n  or describes a change and wants the affected tests identified. Maps changed areas to the\n  tests that exercise them, ranks by risk, and proposes a run set with a rationale — plus a\n  safety net of always-run tests. It recommends; a human confirms before anything is skipped.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Execution\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "regression-suite-selector", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "2e64521fe648a0220060", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/test-execution-tracker/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/test-execution-tracker/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "efa774aecbc870f4320bd462b89b1a8b9b9c819c", "sha256": "612820d9e673a97d56a6b32404d349d6f9f51172a55b8b83f0188c969f61bc6a", "bytes": 2886, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517150+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/test-execution-tracker/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/05-test-execution/test-execution-tracker/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-execution-tracker\ndescription: >-\n  Log and summarize the execution of a test cycle. Use when a tester says \"log this run\",\n  \"track execution for the sprint\", or reports results case by case and wants them recorded.\n  Captures pass / fail / blocked / not-run per case with evidence links and environment,\n  then rolls up progress — completion %, pass rate, blockers. Records only what actually\n  happened; anything unverified is marked \"not run\", never assumed green.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Execution\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-execution-tracker", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "155699dc438d7c4ebc7e", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-reporter/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-reporter/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "100dc6f042f443913242ba6e76d9e1bf300a5422", "sha256": "e8287e5cd2e7267884381045e8c15d8d84f972eb4bb9e4e63d1c7d2ccabe9f54", "bytes": 2866, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517206+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-reporter/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-reporter/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: bug-reporter\ndescription: >-\n  Turn a failure into a clean, reproducible bug report. Use when a tester says \"file a bug\n  for this\", \"write up this defect\", or describes something broken and wants it documented\n  properly. Produces a structured report — title, environment, steps to reproduce, expected\n  vs actual, severity/priority, evidence, and suspected area — ready to paste into the\n  tracker after a human confirms it. Reports only observed facts; never invents a repro step\n  or a log line.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Defect Management\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "bug-reporter", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "84a3a8b73f0021715529", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-triage-assistant/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-triage-assistant/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "be71ed35086cb22de465d6dcca1d7fe7068817fa", "sha256": "bdcb7002e8f29a63bacb6ebb6722560f156f5d392692db2fb38e796a6a09cdcc", "bytes": 2839, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517345+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-triage-assistant/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/bug-triage-assistant/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: bug-triage-assistant\ndescription: >-\n  Triage a batch of defects instead of grinding through them one by one. Use when a lead\n  says \"triage these bugs\", \"prioritize the defect backlog\", or pastes a list of open\n  issues that need sorting. Groups likely duplicates, proposes severity/priority, routes\n  each to a component or owner, and flags reports missing information. Every duplicate and\n  routing is a suggestion for a human to confirm — it never auto-closes or reassigns silently.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Defect Management\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "bug-triage-assistant", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "af83ad5c4f6aeca9c972", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/rca-analyzer/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/rca-analyzer/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "7c00a4949c8886f4316e5d09e61f298186eb51d1", "sha256": "8c768e5af35b2c4e569c797a1658438719783388234909473dcfd54a0123c891", "bytes": 2913, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517458+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/rca-analyzer/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/06-defect-management/rca-analyzer/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: rca-analyzer\ndescription: >-\n  Run a structured root-cause analysis on a defect. Use when someone says \"do an RCA for\n  this bug\", \"why did this escape\", or wants to understand a failure beyond its symptom.\n  Applies 5-Whys and a fishbone across people, process, tooling, data, and environment,\n  separates root cause from symptom, and proposes corrective and preventive actions.\n  Reasons only from evidence supplied; unknown links are marked as hypotheses to verify.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Defect Management\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "rca-analyzer", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "c5dbf9cd50f9c3e20135", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-closure-reporter/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-closure-reporter/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "29cd1e68af3fae80723601b90a1501ee16faca7b", "sha256": "96930f34eb5fdb7ad3c6136e05fa334c7f702536e37f095f28a53cfd0b9470fd", "bytes": 2865, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517542+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-closure-reporter/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-closure-reporter/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-closure-reporter\ndescription: >-\n  Produce the closure report that wraps up a test cycle. Use when a lead says \"write the\n  test closure report\", \"summarize the test cycle\", or needs an end-of-cycle summary for\n  sign-off. Pulls the metrics — pass rate, defect density, open criticals, coverage — into\n  highlights, risks, and a go/no-go recommendation. The recommendation is advisory only:\n  it lays out the evidence, but a human owns the sign-off decision. Uses real numbers, never\n  invented ones.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Closure\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-closure-reporter", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "d71afce82f298115e07e", "repository": "govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files", "commit_sha": "6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69", "skill_path": "stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-coverage-analyzer/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/blob/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-coverage-analyzer/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "b1d9dbf061bd523ea0171fbc6f1e9393e4deb819", "sha256": "c1734226f6c5a4da5e89f7d4eebf1e9e19fbcf0024272b9e7515b5cfd3bf8024", "bytes": 2762, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:41:48.517615+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69/stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-coverage-analyzer/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": [], "repository_manifest": "manifests/govardhanrekha/QA-Skill.md-files/6cef000d8099688b2f34a155adbac44ae5903e69.json", "local_package_files": ["stlc_manual_testing/07-test-closure/test-coverage-analyzer/SKILL.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: test-coverage-analyzer\ndescription: >-\n  Find the gaps between what was required and what was actually tested. Use when a lead\n  says \"where are our coverage gaps\", \"what isn't tested\", or wants requirements and code\n  areas checked against the executed and available tests. Builds a traceability view —\n  requirements/ACs and code areas on one axis, tests on the other — and surfaces untested\n  ACs, thinly covered areas, and orphan tests. Reports gaps from real artifacts, never\n  assumed coverage.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: Rekha Govardhanan\n  stlc-phase: Test Closure\n  version: 1.0.0", "declared_name": "test-coverage-analyzer", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
